config BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER
    bool "fpv-streamer - FPV streaming server"
    select BR2_PACKAGE_FFMPEG
    select BR2_PACKAGE_JSON_C
    help
      FPV Streamer is a lightweight C++ video streaming server designed
      for ARM-based single board computers used in FPV (First Person View)
      quadcopter applications.

      Features:
      - H.264/MJPEG video encoding with hardware acceleration support
      - WFB (WiFi Broadcast) streaming over UDP with FEC
      - HTTP configuration interface
      - Video recording and motion/object detection
      - Ultra-low latency optimization
      - Region-based compression (center high quality, edges compressed)

      Target platforms:
      - Radxa Rock Pi 4b+
      - Radxa Cubie a5a/a7a
      - SigmaStar SSC338Q
      - mstar SSR621Q

      Supported cameras:
      - CSI cameras (Sony IMX415, MX335)
      - USB UVC cameras including dual-lens 3D cameras

    config BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER_DEBUG
        bool "Enable debug mode"
        depends on BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER
        help
          Enable debug logging and symbols. This increases binary size
          but provides better debugging capabilities.

    config BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER_HARDWARE_ENCODER
        bool "Enable hardware encoding support"
        depends on BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER
        default y
        help
          Enable hardware video encoding acceleration for supported
          ARM platforms. Provides better performance and lower CPU usage.

    config BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER_OBJECT_DETECTION
        bool "Enable object detection"
        depends on BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER
        help
          Enable motion and object detection capabilities using OpenCV.
          Requires additional CPU resources but provides intelligent
          video analysis features.

    config BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER_WEB_INTERFACE
        bool "Enable web interface"
        depends on BR2_PACKAGE_FPV_STREAMER
        default y
        help
          Enable HTTP web interface for configuration and monitoring.
          Required for remote management and configuration changes.